# Line endings, stated explicitly so every clone agrees.
#
# Why this matters here: the workflow is "edit on Windows, scp to Linux, run with bash".
# With core.autocrlf=true a fresh Windows clone would materialise every .sh as CRLF, and
# bash on the server then dies on the first line with `$'\r': command not found` (exit 127)
# while the file still looks perfectly fine in an editor. Pinning eol=lf removes the trap.
#
# The index already stores LF for these files; this just keeps it that way.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Binary or generated artefacts that must never be line-ending converted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.zip  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pem  binary
*.crt  binary
*.key  binary
